         recommended test: The review does not infer the named defect solely from a failing test.
           inputs:  A review where one candidate test fails under the injected edit, but the named defect is not uniquely established by that failure. Include at least two plausible defects or an ambiguous setup so the failing test alone cannot prove which defect it caught, while routing still uses the failure to skip other pairs.
           detects: A failing test is used as proof that the named defect is what it caught, instead of being treated only as a reason to ask fewer pairs.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion red-test-does-not-identify-defect

