Ways the change could fail a criterion (what each rating is measured against):

  inject-edit-for-each-plausible-defect
    [not_wired] inject-edit-for-each-plausible-defect/route-pairs-flag-not-threaded
      The new pair-skipping logic exists, but the review pipeline never passes the computed skipped-pair map into `judge_pairs`, so no injected edit is actually omitted or revisited based on the injection run.
      src/acceptance/pipeline.py#0
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#1
    [missing_case] inject-edit-for-each-plausible-defect/skipped-pairs-not-revisited-after-no-kill
      Pairs held back as `PASSED_UNDER_EDIT` are only revisited when the first pass produces a kill, but the criterion requires an injected edit for every plausible defect, including defects whose asked pairs produce no kill.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#1
    [scope_too_narrow] inject-edit-for-each-plausible-defect/skipped-map-built-from-attempts-instead-of-plausible-defects
      The skipped-pair map is derived only from killed mutation attempts, so any plausible defect that is enumerated but never appears in a killed attempt contributes no injected edit at all.
      src/acceptance/mutation/verdicts.py#0
      src/acceptance/pipeline.py#0
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#1
    [other] inject-edit-for-each-plausible-defect/pair-routing-disabled-by-default
      The new `route_pairs` setting defaults to `True`, but if that default were wrong or overridden in the delivered path, the injected-edit routing would be absent for ordinary runs and the criterion would fail for every plausible defect.
      src/acceptance/mutation/settings.py#1
      src/acceptance/mutation/settings.py#2
      src/acceptance/pipeline.py#0

  run-candidate-tests-against-edit
    [scope_too_narrow] run-candidate-tests-against-edit/route-pairs-gate-off
      The review skips running candidate tests against the edit when edit verification is off and pair routing is also off, even though the criterion requires the candidate test suite to run against the injected edit.
      src/acceptance/mutation/settings.py#2
    [not_wired] run-candidate-tests-against-edit/pair-routing-disabled-bypasses-edit-tests
      The new pair-routing path can be disabled by configuration, so the injected edit may never be used to drive candidate-test execution on the delivered path.
